(A value is compared by order once it has been checked with 'is a number' and put in a number variable. Equality on a value is unchanged, and a value retyped in place compares as the number it now holds.)

To 'measure' with a number called sensor.
    If sensor is 0, Return a value, "offline".
    Return a value, sensor multiply 10.

a value called measurement is 'measure' of 4.
a number called level is 0.
If measurement is a number, Set level to measurement.
If level is greater than 30 then, Print "high".
Otherwise, Print "low".

a value called silence is 'measure' of 0.
If silence is a number, Print "a number".
Otherwise, Print "not a number".
If silence is "offline" then, Print "offline".

a value called count is "357".
count is a number.
If count is greater than or equal to 300, Print "357 is 300 or more".
